# `web/` itself is NOT excluded — the image builds the dashboard from source in its own
# stage. Only the two directories that must never enter the context are:
#
#   node_modules  hundreds of megabytes, platform-specific, and rebuilt by `npm ci`
#                 anyway. Copying a host's tree in would also risk native modules built
#                 for the wrong platform silently overriding the container's.
#   web/dist      a stale local build. If this were copied in, the image would serve
#                 whatever was last built on a developer's machine rather than what the
#                 `web` stage produces from the committed source — which is exactly the
#                 drift that building in the image is meant to eliminate.
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/coverage/
